                <pb facs="0139" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-17T16:00:00-03:00">December 17, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2094. For the Under Secretary. Aranha tells me that the Canadian Minister
                    approached him in connection with the possibility of having Canada invited to
                    the meeting of Foreign Ministers. Aranha referred him to Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
